{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"A Chariot","html":"<article id='sn1.72'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.72 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.72 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>8. Chetvāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>8. Slain </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Rathasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A Chariot </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kiṁsu rathassa paññāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“What is a chariot known by? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsu paññāṇamaggino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What is fire known by? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kiṁsu raṭṭhassa paññāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What is a nation known by? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsu paññāṇamitthiyā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What is a woman known by?” </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dhajo rathassa paññāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“A chariot is known by a banner. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhūmo paññāṇamaggino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Fire is known by smoke. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Rājā raṭṭhassa paññāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A nation is known by its ruler. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhattā paññāṇamitthiyā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A woman is known by her husband.” </span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
